    },
    {
      "key": "blog_detail_4fac5cef0a97",
      "text": "When someone searches for “brunch near me” or “Italian food in [Your City],” Google is trying to serve them a result that’s relevant, close by, and well-reviewed. That’s the core of local SEO. It’s not just about your website, it’s about sending Google clear, consistent signals that your restaurant is a great match for local diners.\n\nAnd the homepage? It’s one of the most important places to do that.\nThis guide walks you through the most critical (and often overlooked) ways to optimize your restaurant homepage so you’re showing up when and where it matters most: right in your neighborhood.",
